  - id: folsom
    name: Folsom
    county: Sacramento County
    blurb: Folsom homes range from historic properties near Sutter Street to hillside houses with wood stoves and inserts. Cap and spark arrestor checks are a smart addition for homes near open space.
  - id: citrus-heights
    name: Citrus Heights
    county: Sacramento County
    blurb: Many Citrus Heights homes date from the 1960s–1980s and have original masonry fireplaces, which can mean aging mortar, worn dampers and crowns due for attention.
  - id: rancho-cordova
    name: Rancho Cordova
    county: Sacramento County
    blurb: Rancho Cordova has both mid-century homes with original brick chimneys and newer communities with gas fireplaces. We clean, inspect and repair both.
  - id: carmichael
    name: Carmichael
    county: Sacramento County
    blurb: Carmichael's larger lots and mature trees are beautiful, but leaves and branches can clog chimney caps and spark arrestors, and nests are common in uncapped flues.
  - id: fair-oaks
    name: Fair Oaks
    county: Sacramento County
    blurb: Fair Oaks has many established homes with wood-burning fireplaces and stoves. Regular sweeping and inspections keep them safe to use through the winter.
  - id: orangevale
    name: Orangevale
    county: Sacramento County
    blurb: On Orangevale's semi-rural properties, wood stoves are popular. We service stoves, stovepipes and chimneys, and install spark arrestors.
